@400 = ~Branwen Spiritual Hammer: repair magical-weapon charges~
@410 = ~Yeslick and Keldorn Dispel Magic: hostile-only, correctly scaled dispels~
@430 = ~Scrolls: use the reader's active caster level, or half their active class level~
@1430 = ~Reader-level scroll casting requires a supported Windows BG2EE/EET engine with EEex. Other engine ABIs are not supported by this native runtime.~
@1431 = ~Reader-level scroll casting requires EEex. Install EEex before this component.~
@1432 = ~The scroll runtime package is incomplete: CBMScroll.dll or CBMSPolicy.exe is missing. Use a complete modpack package.~
@1433 = ~The installed scroll inventory could not be built safely. Read the policy builder's diagnostic above; no runtime was installed.~
@1434 = ~Some scroll abilities retain native behavior because their installed spell graph needs review. The builder lists each resource and reason; the complete report is CBMScroll/CBMSPOL1.json.~
@1435 = ~Reader-level scroll casting installed. Genuine fixed protection scrolls and manual learning retain their normal behavior. Install this component after spell/item changes; reinstall it if those resources change. Native game acceptance remains pending.~
@440 = ~Ascension Improved Slayer Transformation: repair EE Fixpack subspell links~
@450 = ~SCS shapechange spells: repair the EE Fixpack interaction~

@610 = ~Progressive XP for locks, traps and spell scribing (multiclass/dual-class aware; requires EEex)~
@1610 = ~Progressive utility XP requires BG2:EE or EET.~
@1611 = ~Progressive utility XP requires EEex. Install EEex first and launch through InfinityLoader.~
@1612 = ~Progressive utility XP requires XPBONUS.2DA and XPLEVEL.2DA.~
@1613 = ~[CBM utility XP] Installed. Edit override/CBMUXPC.lua to tune rewards, then restart the game. See docs/utility-xp.md.~
@611 = ~Story-based utility XP: BG1 rewards through SoD, BG2 rewards from SoA (requires EET and EEex)~
@1614 = ~Choose one utility-XP mode: story-based 611 or progressive 610. Uninstall the other mode before switching.~
@1615 = ~Story-based utility XP requires EET. Standalone games and other campaign systems are unsupported.~
@1616 = ~Story-based utility XP requires EEex. Install EEex first and launch through InfinityLoader.~
@1617 = ~Story-based utility XP requires XPBONUS.2DA.~
@1618 = ~[CBM story utility XP] Installed. Locks, traps and scribing use BG1-sized rewards throughout BG1 and SoD, then native BG2 rewards from SoA onward. See docs/story-utility-xp.md for level brackets and the BG1 lock typo correction.~

@199 = ~EET companion continuity: preserve the original Xan and Yeslick across campaigns (NEW GAME, BEFORE EET_end)~
@188 = ~BG1 Yeslick: Fighter/Alaghor of Clangeddin (requires YeslickNPC Alaghor, BEFORE 199/EET_end)~
