@630 = ~Generic artwork for unidentified items (requires EEex)~
@1630 = ~Generic unidentified-item artwork currently supports BG2EE and EET on Windows.~
@1631 = ~Install EEex / InfinityLoader first. This component needs its loader database and the Windows game executable.~
@1632 = ~Choose one unidentified-item appearance option: generic artwork or Randomiser's cursed-item appearance. Ordinary loot randomization can stay installed.~
@1633 = ~Generic unidentified-item artwork installed. Launch with InfinityLoader. Identifying an item restores its own artwork; item abilities, text and saves are unchanged.~
@640 = ~Legacy UI text compatibility for LeUI and Dragonspear UI~
@1640 = ~Legacy UI text compatibility supports BG2:EE and EET.~
@1641 = ~Legacy UI text compatibility requires UTIL.LUA from the game. Install the UI provider before this component.~
@1642 = ~Legacy UI text compatibility installed. Install after the UI provider and before Bubb's Spell Menu. An existing working t() helper is preserved.~

@660 = ~Degrodel: hand over the Helm of Balduran or keep it and fight him~
@1660 = ~Degrodel's Helm of Balduran choice supports BG:EE and EET.~
@1661 = ~Degrodel's dialog DEGROD.DLG is missing, so the Helm of Balduran quest is not available in this game.~
@1662 = ~Here is the helm, as we agreed.~
@1663 = ~No. The Helm of Balduran stays with us.~
@1664 = ~You would cheat me? Fools! Then I shall take the helm from your corpses!~
@1665 = ~The Helm of Balduran
I refused to hand the Helm of Balduran over to Degrodel. Rather than let us leave with it, the wizard and his servants attacked us.~
@1666 = ~Degrodel's Helm of Balduran choice skipped: DEGROD.DLG is not a valid dialog (%cbm_dgf_reason%). Nothing was changed.~
@1667 = ~Degrodel's Helm of Balduran choice skipped: no transition in DEGROD.DLG takes the Helm of Balduran (HELM07) from the party and leaves the area. Nothing was changed.~
@1668 = ~Degrodel's Helm of Balduran choice skipped: DEGROD.DLG has %cbm_dgf_matches% Helm of Balduran hand-ins (states%cbm_dgf_match_states%), so the one to extend is ambiguous. Nothing was changed.~
@1669 = ~Degrodel's Helm of Balduran choice skipped: the hand-in state %cbm_dgf_state% in DEGROD.DLG also continues without a player reply (for example into a companion interjection). Adding replies there would change that transition. Nothing was changed.~
@1670 = ~Degrodel's Helm of Balduran choice is already present in DEGROD.DLG. Nothing was changed.~
@1671 = ~Degrodel's Helm of Balduran choice skipped: the hand-in actions in DEGROD.DLG state %cbm_dgf_state% could not be separated into individual actions. Nothing was changed.~
@1672 = ~Degrodel's Helm of Balduran choice installed at DEGROD.DLG state %cbm_dgf_state%. Refusing creates the hand-in's %cbm_dgf_n_servants% servant(s), closes its %cbm_dgf_n_journal% open journal entr(ies), and leaves out:%cbm_dgf_dropped%.~

@650 = ~Campaign XP caps - keep excess XP for later (BG1/SoD; experimental)~
@651 = ~Campaign XP caps - also cap SoA until ToB (requires 650; experimental)~
@1650 = ~Campaign XP banking requires Enhanced Edition Trilogy (EET).~
@1651 = ~Campaign XP banking requires the Windows x64 game and EEex/InfinityLoader native modules. Install EEex first; startup also verifies the reviewed native interfaces.~
@1652 = ~Campaign XP banking requires the installed XPLEVEL.2DA progression table.~
@1653 = ~Experimental campaign XP component installed; game testing is still pending. Install after 237/238/620 if selected, keep the mod folder, and restart through InfinityLoader. See docs/campaign-xp-banking.md. This does not repair existing saves.~
@1654 = ~Install Campaign XP caps component 650 before its SoA option.~
@1655 = ~Experimental SoA cap option installed. The setting applies when a character first gets a banking account; it does not change saved banking settings. Uninstalling 651 restores the BG1/SoD installer setting.~
